          %title
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong Schneider’s descent theorem
            is a noncommutative affine analogue of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+along+a+torsor"} descent along a torsor
            where the structure group is also replaced by a Hopf algebra.
          %h2#the_theorem The theorem
          %h3#preliminaries Preliminaries
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            be a Hopf algebra with comultiplication
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi E
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = (E,\rho_E:E\to E\otimes H)
            a right
            = succeed "-comodule" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi co
                      %mi H
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = E^{co H}\subset E
            of coinvariants. Consider the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %msup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_E\mathcal{M}^H
            of relative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+modules"} Hopf modules
            and the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_U\mathcal{M}
            of left
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            Taking coinvariants extends to a functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi co
                        %mi H
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %msup
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ()^{co H}:{}_E\mathcal{M}^H\to {}_U\mathcal{M}
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi U
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\otimes_U M
            is canonically a relative Hopf module via coaction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi U
                  %mi m
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi U
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\otimes_U m\mapsto (e_{(0)}\otimes_U m)\otimes e_{(1)}
            and the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi U
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\mapsto E\otimes_U M
            extends to a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi U
                  %mo −
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %msup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\otimes_U -:{}_U\mathcal{M}\to {}_E\mathcal{M}^H
            which is adjoint to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi co
                        %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ()^{co H}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi N
                    %mo :
                    %mi N
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi U
                    %mi N
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi co
                        %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_N : N\mapsto (E\otimes_U N)^{co H}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ↦
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi U
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\mapsto 1\otimes_U n
            and the counit is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi M
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi U
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mi co
                        %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_M:E\otimes_U M^{co H}\to M
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi U
                    %mi m
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi e
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\otimes_U m\mapsto e m
          %h3#statement Statement
          %p
            In the left-right version, it says that given a Hopf algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            and a faithfully flat right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf-Galois+extension"} Hopf-Galois extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\hookrightarrow E
            which is faithfully flat from the left, the category of left-right relative Hopf modules
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %msup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_E\mathcal{M}^H
            is equivalent to the category of left
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_U \mathcal{M}
            via the adjoint equivalence described above.
          %p
            Schneider proves the equivalence for left-left Hopf modules, hence he needs an additional assumption that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            has a bijective antipode.
          %h3#modern_proofs Modern proofs
          %p
            Schneider’s original proof is rather involved. Modern proofs begin by rephrasing the category of relative Hopf modules in different terms, either as modules over certain cosimplicial algebra (“coBorel construction” by Lunts-Škoda 2002, see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#ŠkodaGMJ2009"} ŠkodaGMJ2009
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on the category of
            = succeed "-modules," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "-coring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi U
                  %mi E
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\otimes_U E\cong E\otimes H
            directly gives the equivalence of any of the three constructions with the analogue in the descent theory for extension of rings; for example the Sweedler coring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi U
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\otimes_U E
            is isomorphic to the mentioned coring. Hence the categories of comodules are equivalent and the theorem hence boils down to the standard faithfully flat descent (for noncommutative rings) or comonadicity criterium in comonadic version.
          %p
            Let us describe the comonad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on the category of left
            = succeed "-modules," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_E\mathcal{M}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            sends a left
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\otimes H
            with
            = succeed "-coaction" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                    %mi M
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \id_M\otimes\Delta:M\otimes H\to (M\otimes H)\otimes H
            and left
            = succeed "-action," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi m
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi h
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\otimes (m\otimes h) = \sum e_{(0)} m\otimes e_{(1)} h.
          %p
            (Remark: This action is induced by a distributive law.) The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            of this comonad is equivalent to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %msup
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_E\mathcal{M}^H
          %h2#literature Literature
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans-J%C3%BCrgen+Schneider"}> Hans-Jürgen Schneider
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Principal homogeneous spaces for arbitrary Hopf algebras
              %p
                Israel J. Math.
                %strong 72
                (1990), no. 1-2, 167–195
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1098988"} MR92a:16047
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02764619"} doi
            %li{:id => "ŠkodaGMJ2009"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Z.+%C5%A0koda"}> Z. Škoda
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Some equivariant constructions in noncommutative algebraic geometry
              %strong 16
              (2009), No. 1, 183–202,
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0811.4770"} arXiv:0811.4770
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2527623"} MR2011b:14004
          %p A generalization to Hopf algebroids is proven in
          %ul
            %li
              A. Ardizzoni,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G.+B%C3%B6hm"} G. Böhm
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Schneider type theorem for Hopf algebroids
              %strong 318
              (2007), no. 1, 225–269
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2363132"} MR2008j:16103
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jalgebra.2007.05.017"} doi
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0612633"} math.QA/0612633
              (arXiv version is unified, corrected);
              = succeed "," do
                %em Corrigendum
              = succeed ":6" do
                %strong 321
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2498268"} MR2010b:16060
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jalgebra.2008.11.040"} doi
